  "instructions": "Product Designer and Frontend Engineer use the same full design skill library, versions and reference files. Every full file stays available in the shared project and the Cloud workspace; available does not mean loaded. Follow the precedence in studio-design-gate: YC Interface Craft leads visual direction (read its SKILL.md and only the 3-5 matching research records); Intentional UI Design sets the quality floor; frontend-design guides composition and type. Load Illustration Design Grammar, motion (Emil design engineering and the animation skills) and component references only when the chosen design needs them, and record that choice in the design contract. product-marketing, copywriting, copy-editing and conversion guidance shape the copy. A link or summary is not a loaded skill. Use design-skill-library.json to compare file hashes and preserve licenses. Do not load unrelated native-app guidance. Frontend keeps its engineering, SEO, build and test skills. It implements the contracted type, spacing, color, imagery, interaction and motion as components written for this page. Do not invent a new direction or repeat exploration after approval. Record the paths actually read in evidence/design-skills-read.md. The Designer and a marketing reviewer pass Gate 1 and Gate 2 on actual screenshots before the owner review.",
